      "text": "\\boxed{}\n\nTo find the volume of the frustum, we first need to determine the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid. The volume \\( V \\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height} \\]\n\nThe original pyramid has a base edge of 12 cm and an altitude of 8 cm. Therefore, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times (12 \\times 12) \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe smaller pyramid has a base edge of 6 cm and an altitude of 4 cm. Therefore, the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times (6 \\times 6) \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
