      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We know that the volume \\( V \\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot B \\cdot h \\]\nwhere \\( B \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the pyramid.\n\nFor the original pyramid:\n\\[ B_{\\text{original}} = 12 \\cdot 12 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\\[ h_{\\text{original}} = 8 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 144 \\cdot 8 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nFor the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ B_{\\text{smaller}} = 6 \\cdot 6 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\\[ h_{\\text{smaller}} = 4 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\\[ V_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 36 \\cdot 4 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nLet's use the Python code to verify these calculations.\n\n```python\n# Define the base edge lengths and altitudes\nbase_edge_original = 12\nbase_edge_smaller = 6\naltitude_original = 8\naltitude_smaller = 4\n\n# Calculate the areas of the bases\nbase_area_original = base_edge_original ** 2\nbase_area_small = base_edge_smaller ** 2\n\n# Calculate the volumes of the pyramids\nvolume_original = (1/3) * base_area_original * altitude_original\nvolume_small = (1/3) * base_area_small * altitude_smaller\n\n# Calculate the volume of the frustum\nvolume_frustum = volume_original - volume_small\n\n# Output the volume of the frustum\nprint(volume_frustum)\n```\n```output\n336.0\n```\nThe volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.",
