      "text": "1. **Volume of the Larger Pyramid:**\n   - The volume of the larger pyramid can be calculated using the formula for the volume of a pyramid:\n     \\[\n     V_{\\text{large pyramid}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height}\n     \\]\n     Given that the base edge of the larger pyramid is 12 cm, the base area is:\n     \\[\n     12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\n     \\]\n     And the height is 8 cm:\n     \\[\n     V_{\\text{large pyramid}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1152}{3} = 384 \\text{ cm}^3\n     \\]\n\n2. **Volume of the Smaller Pyramid:**\n   - Similarly, the base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm, so the base area is:\n     \\[\n     6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n     \\]\n   - The smaller pyramid shares the same height (4 cm) as the larger pyramid:\n     \\[\n     V_{\\text{smaller pyramid}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3\n     \\]\n\n3. **Volume of the Frustum:**\n   - The volume of the frustum is the total volume of the larger pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n     \\[\n     V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{large pyramid}} - V_{\\text{smaller pyramid}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3\n     \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\nTherefore, the volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.",
