      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we will subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the original pyramid.\n\nFirst, let's find the volume of the original pyramid. The formula for the volume of a pyramid is:\n\nV = (1/3) * base area * height\n\nThe base area of the original pyramid is 12 cm * 12 cm = 144 cm², and the height is 8 cm. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\nV_original = (1/3) * 144 cm² * 8 cm = 384 cm³\n\nNext, let's find the volume of the smaller pyramid. We know that the smaller pyramid has a base edge of 6 cm and an altitude of 4 cm, and its base area is 6 cm * 6 cm = 36 cm². Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\nV_smaller = (1/3) * 36 cm² * 4 cm = 48 cm³\n\nNow, we will subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid to find the volume of the frustum:\n\nV_frustum = V_original - V_smaller = 384 cm³ - 48 cm³ = 336 cm³\n\nTherefore, there are \\boxed{336} cubic centimeters in the volume of the frustum.",
